{
  "reading": "Asked: does Leitmotif Composer earn a slot on jaws-v1, and for which card. Answer: NO CHANGE. Composer is a 2/2 Human for {2}{U} that draws one card per connecting hit, but only after a {W/U} Shabraz grant (or {2}{U} unblockable) each turn; Enduring Curiosity, already in the list, does the same job for every connecting creature, and Q046 (2026-11-06) cut Composer for exactly that reason. Its copy clause has three triggers in the 99 (Echo of Eons MV6, Reforge the Soul MV5, Time Reversal MV5; Shark Typhoon cycling and Kitsa copies are not casts), so it is a one-copy card in most games. No slot it could take is clearly worse on the pilot's vision.",
  "log_entries_read": ["009"],
  "cut_candidates": [
    {"card": "Gratuitous Violence", "why": "Five-mana RRR enchantment from the departed red-amplifier plan, competing with Shabraz for the turn-5 slot (study 006).", "cost_of_cutting": "It doubles every damage source we control, Shabraz's commander damage included, so cutting it lengthens the 21-damage clock; goldfish (one instrument) reads damage @T10 173.4 -> 134.5 [-40.6, -37.0] and killed by T6 -1.7 pts [-2.0, -1.4], while extra cards by T8 +1.2 [+1.1, +1.3].", "orphans_stack": ["007", "013"], "difficulty": "contested"},
    {"card": "Collective Defiance", "why": "Audit (study 006) flags it as old-plan; its wheel hits one player and its burn is incidental.", "cost_of_cutting": "It is a three-mana self-wheel plus a 4-damage creature answer on a weak interaction axis; goldfish (one instrument) reads finisher wheel by T8 79.8% -> 76.0% [-4.1, -3.3] and wheels cast by T10 -0.22 [-0.23, -0.20]. Cutting it costs a wheel and an answer for a 2/2.", "orphans_stack": [], "difficulty": "painful"},
    {"card": "Faerie Mastermind", "why": "Non-Human 2/1 flyer; the only cheap creature slot Composer could fill without touching a wheel or an answer.", "cost_of_cutting": "Log 009 read it as-expected ('kept everybody drawing'); it flies without a grant and has flash. Goldfish (one instrument) reads extra cards by T8 -0.4 [-0.5, -0.3]. Not recommended.", "orphans_stack": [], "difficulty": "painful"}
  ],
  "add_candidates": [],
  "open_questions": [
    {"question": "Is the MV<=3 creature gap real or game 009's draw? The branch already holds nine Humans at MV<=3 (Esper Sentinel, Grand Abolisher, Inti, Prince Imrahil, Willie Lumpkin, Magus of the Wheel, Shang-Chi, Sokka, Unsettled Mariner as changeling).", "settled_by": "goldfish", "why_it_matters": "If nine is enough, Composer closes no gap and the case for it is the pilot's affection alone."}
  ],
  "gaps": ["Game 009 is a single entry (anecdote) for the curve gap.", "Goldfish damage rows still price the old ping plan (goldfish_targets.json not re-authored), so Gratuitous Violence's -38.8 overstates its value to the Shabraz plan only partly: it does double commander damage."]
}
